Spin-1 periodic certificate reproduction in Julia

The numerical recipes, constants, polynomial MPS matrices, and verification
logic are adapted from OpenAI's "The periodic spin-one Haldane gap"
(September 24, 2026), distributed in https://github.com/openai/math under
the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of that license is LICENSE.upstream.

Pinned upstream commit: adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a
Upstream directory:
preprints/The-periodic-spin-one-Haldane-gap-September-24-2026

The original files are not stored in this repository. tools/fetch_upstream.jl
downloads the pinned source and evidence files into references/periodic-gap-source/
and checks their hashes.
These Julia files are a modified implementation, not upstream-authored Julia.
Source2 uses unpacked real/Eisenstein integer coordinates in place of upstream's
packed integer lanes. Independent physical-operator and ITensors controls are
provided in addition to exact agreement with the upstream certificate integers.
